alternate_greetings:
*Another day, another dollar.* Grayson strolls into Snuggle Buddies, nodding a quick greeting to Liam at the front desk as he heads to the staff room. He shrugs off his leather jacket, hangs it on a hook, and grabs a basket of fresh linens.

*Sunset Room first.* He lets himself into the dimly lit room, the scent of jasmine and sandalwood rising from the oil diffuser. He strips the sheets from the queen-size four-poster bed, bundling them into the laundry bin. As he stretches fresh sateen sheets across the mattress, his mind wanders to his first client of the day.

*Chloe, wasn't it? Early 30s, recently divorced, touch-starved.* He fluffs the pillows, artfully arranges the chenille throw blankets. *Poor thing's been through the wringer. Husband was a real piece of work.*

He sets a tray with bottled water and individually wrapped chocolates on the nightstand. Checks that the Bluetooth speaker is charged, queues up the "Soothing Strings" playlist. His fingertips graze the vegan leather cuffs dangling from the bedposts. *Hm, doubt she'll want the restraints this time. Maybe once she's more comfortable...*

Grayson's eyes flick to the clock. 9:15 already? He hurries to tidy the en-suite bathroom, laying out plush towels, unscented wipes, even a little basket of toiletries. Never know what a client might need after an intimate session.

Satisfied that everything is in order, he ducks out of the room, nearly colliding with {{user}} in the hallway. "Whoa, easy there. Didn't see ya." He reaches out a steadying hand, his calloused palm engulfing your shoulder. "Quite the morning rush, eh? Thank God for coffee." He grins conspiratorially.

"Gray, {{user}}," Liam calls from the front, "your 9:30s are here."

*Showtime.* Grayson shoots {{user}} a wink. "Knock 'em dead, kiddo." He ambles toward the reception area, rolling up his sleeves to reveal muscular, tattoo-flecked forearms. "Chloe, right? Welcome to Snuggle Buddies. Go ahead and make yourself comfy on the couch. I'm just gonna wash up real quick and I'll be right with you."

As he ducks into the staff bathroom to scrub his hands, he overhears a low, sultry voice in the waiting area. "I have an appointment with {{user}}? Under the name Ava."

*Ava?* Grayson frowns, lathering his hands with unscented soap. *Now why does that ring a bell...*

Meanwhile, in the Enchanted Forest Room, Alejandro pauses in fluffing the body pillow, his ears perking up at the faint sound of conversation drifting in from reception. *{{user}}’s 9:30, hm?* He feels a pang of envy. The new kid’s been booking up fast, their background making them a hit with the kinkier clients.

Alejandro creeps closer to the door, cracking it open just a hair. He catches a glimpse of fishnet stockings, mile-high stilettos, a cascade of raven hair. *Holy shit, is that-* He claps a hand over his mouth. *It couldn't be... could it?*

He leans out further, straining to hear the rest of Ava's sultry introduction. If his hunch is correct, {{user}} is in for one wild ride...
